    "body": "## What and why\n\nAdd an opt-in direct legal-set constructor inside the existing protected native Prefix/Generate transaction. The prior residual-feedback constructor offered no protected descending update. This mechanism jointly selects among all 15 legal destinations for all 1,920 original master coordinates under the same 380 saved guard rows. Fractional no-op bits, independent actual-displacement screening, native CE/reference/guard checks, restage, atomic commit and reload remain authoritative. The pure-Rust solver is offline tooling only.\n\n## Result\n\n**KEEP the implementation and execution evidence; constructor NOT YET PROMOTED.** The absolute-code and mathematically equivalent centered-displacement attempts both returned `InternalError(\"Singular matrix\")` without an assignment or native proposal. The backend supplied no failing basis, phase, node count or iteration count. This is unavailable model-quality evidence, not infeasibility, a model negative, or an optimal no-op.\n\nBoth attempts reused the exact #2101 saved derivatives, with zero new training graphs/backwards. Each enclosing pipeline exported and independently reloaded the unchanged original input245 artifact: 5/15 conditional winners including EOS, 17/17 references and 380/380 protected winners over the 391-row union. Initial and final objective records are exactly equal within and across attempts. Actual-nine, full512 and fresh qualification are NOT_RUN. Accepted Source48/Generate64 remains 8/512 complete development replies; the separate conditional 9/15 artifact is unchanged.\n\nThe initial run took 145.492 s / peak RSS 1,663,795,200 bytes; the centered run 143.247 s / 1,795,555,328 bytes. Both used 1,960 variables / 440 constraints, unchanged 4096 branch-node bound excluding the root, zero-margin target and original norm-tolerant actual-bit screen. Centering changes only the affine variable representation. Its failure rules out this repair alone as sufficient; the underlying basis defect remains unlocalized. No third blind retry.\n\nExact report/config/binary/source identities, complete verified iCloud archive indexes and source/saved-result reviews are in `docs/labs/direct-legal-construction-2026-10-09/`. The superseded absolute implementation is retained as a full patch plus INDEX row. Next: capture the exact failing LP basis/factorization context from the saved problem before choosing a numerical/backend repair, preserving every constraint.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Exact-source optimized build and 53 focused coupled tests passed; final-head source equality/tests and review posted separately\n- [x] Dated research record, both sealed attempt receipts and retained failure correction\n- [x] Newest-first current-state entry ending in **Next:**\n- [x] Stale-document search; crate README, historical follow-through, geometry role and regenerated figure updated\n- [x] STATUS / ROADMAP / #2028 unchanged: accepted artifact and milestone state unchanged\n- [x] README updated in its existing Training section for this offline mechanism and limitation\n- [x] Claim wording and 29/29 geometry connection checks pass\n- [x] Protected merge 50630b4eb verified on fresh origin/main: all 26 delivered blobs match; GitHub/local branch and owned worktree removed; both full attempts verified in iCloud; hygiene --apply completed and other labs preserved\n\nReferences #2030\n",
